    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0936" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/2–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-20T20:00:00-04:00">February 20,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. The Department has been asked by other agencies to ascertain your views
                    concerning the following points and any others of interest related to the
                    negotiations for sugar, molasses and alcohol: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Present effectiveness of, and future prospects for, Cuban price
                            control for use in consideration of this Government’s justification in
                            undertaking price stabilization program proposed in U.S. memorandum of
                            November 11 last year.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d759-f1"/>
                        </item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Present attitude of Colonos toward United States proposal of November
                            11, as modified perhaps by agreement with Hacendados concerning molasses
                            split.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Adequate realization by Cubans that 3.00 cents is top price.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
